			<div class="content" id="post-content-1966703">
									

<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2550 is most often observed sighing, suggesting moderate emotional distress, if its vocalizations thematically resemble human meanings.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I want to point this sentence out. For starters, it's already stated further up in the description that the bird doesn't seem to be more intelligent than normal for its species, so this supposition would be counterindicated.</p>
<p>lol big words</p>
<p>Speaking narratively, whether or not the thing is actually vocalizing its own emotions is immaterial; it'd be a whole lot better if you just let those vocalization patterns be mentioned through the article, creating the story, than telling us what they mean. In other words, let the reader draw their own conclusion as to what, if anything, the vocalizations mean.</p>

